<h1>Cisco Secure Tokens Commercial Framework (Dual Procurement Paths)</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Framework for enterprise and neocloud motions: direct Cisco procurement through Solutions+ / GPL, or direct platform activation with quarterly/half-year partner settlement. Cisco acts as merchant of record for all Secure Token transactions.</p>

<div class="intro-note">
Equinix already has both selling motions in place today: enterprise-led Cisco procurement and platform-led activation with reconciliation. Cisco Secure Tokens adapts that dual-motion model for secure enterprise access to approved AI models.
</div>

<div class="strip">
    <span>Enterprise Seller Motion</span>
    <span>Neocloud Platform Motion</span>
    <span>BYOL Support</span>
    <span>Merchant of Record</span>
    <span>Q / H Partner Settlement</span>
</div>

<h2>Path A — Enterprise-Led Procurement (Cisco Direct Motion)</h2>
<p>Enterprise account sellers position and sell Cisco Secure Tokens through Solutions+ / GPL, attach Cisco SD-WAN, security, switching, and Galileo, and support BYOL portability into target neocloud and frontier environments (Diamond Tier).</p>
<ol>
    <li>Cisco AE identifies AI / Neocloud use case and proposes reference architecture.</li>
    <li>Enterprise procures Cisco Secure Tokens via Solutions+ / GPL and selects Cisco SD-WAN / security components.</li>
    <li>Cisco SD-WAN, security, and switching deployed; policy, segmentation, and Galileo configured for Neocloud / Frontier model access.</li>
    <li>BYOL enabled: enterprise can apply existing eligible Cisco licenses to supported deployments.</li>
    <li>Enterprise consumes model access — Diamond Tier (OpenAI / Anthropic Claude), plus Platinum / Gold — with Cisco-led commercial attribution at sale.</li>
</ol>

<div class="buying-programs">
<p><strong>Enterprise Buying Programs (Micro Segment):</strong> Align procurement to existing buying constructs to simplify approvals and expand attach.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>EA's:</strong> Use enterprise agreement structures for predictable token consumption.</li>
    <li><strong>WPAS:</strong> Use approved buying pathways to streamline Secure Tokens + SD-WAN acquisition cycles.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<h2>Path B — Neocloud / Platform Direct Activation (Settlement Motion)</h2>
<p>End customer activates Cisco Secure Token consumption directly within Neocloud / inferencing marketplaces, including partners such as Qumulus, Cirrascale, and Massed Compute (Platinum and Gold Tiers).</p>
<ol>
    <li>Customer signs up with Neocloud provider (e.g., Qumulus, Cirrascale, Massed Compute).</li>
    <li>Customer enables Cisco Secure Token consumption from provider catalog. Provider must be qualified (Cisco SD-WAN, Galileo, full Cisco switching).</li>
    <li>BYOL option: customer brings eligible existing Cisco licenses where supported by the platform model.</li>
    <li>Usage / subscription data is mapped to eligible token, model, and infrastructure attribution rules.</li>
    <li>Cisco (merchant of record) executes partner settlement — compensating the model builder and neocloud — at end of quarter or half-year per partner agreement.</li>
</ol>

